  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "AI chat agents for AIChatField (namespace Codeer.LowCode.Blazor.Extras.Server.AI.Chat). IAIChatAgent is the contract; AIChatJobStore runs an agent in the background and answers the field's polling (it takes an agent-name-to-agent table, so no DI registration is required). RawDataAccessAgent talks to any Microsoft.Extensions.AI IChatClient (Azure OpenAI, OpenAI, Ollama...), keeps per-conversation history keyed by the signed-in user and the conversation id, streams partial replies, and trims history (tool results are dropped from older turns, then by turn count and character budget) to keep token usage bounded; prompt and history limits are RawDataAccessOptions, the logger is a constructor argument. RawDataAccessAgent answers questions about the application's data: it reads the application design (list_modules / describe_module: fields with display names, candidate values, links with join keys, logical-delete columns, scripts and page URLs), reads the supplementary documents selected by the field's DocumentFolder, queries one or more data sources with read-only SQL (a two-level get_schema that returns a table index first and columns only for the requested tables; execute_sql limited to a single SELECT with row/character/time limits and an audit log; SQL dialect per data source), and renders bar/line/pie charts as SVG on the server so numbers are never transcribed by the model. Records in a reply link to their CLB detail page. Access control is done on the database side: point the agent at a data source whose connection uses a read-only DB user (or views) that exposes only the tables and columns the AI may read; the library does not decide permissions. User-facing texts (progress, errors) are localized (en, ja-JP); prompts are Japanese. See docs/AIChatField.md in the repository. Requires Codeer.LowCode.Blazor 1.3.32 or later.",
